&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="the-pipeline"&gt;The pipeline&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="the-pipeline"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#the-pipeline" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/CircleCI-Labs/smarter-workflows/blob/main/examples/demo/.circleci/config.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;.circleci/config.yml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the setup config. It builds the planner from this repository, plans &lt;a href="https://github.com/CircleCI-Labs/smarter-workflows/blob/main/examples/demo/.circleci/continue.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;.circleci/continue.yml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (workflow &lt;code&gt;demo&lt;/code&gt;) and continues the pipeline with the result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Job&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Reads&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;lint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the source of the three services and the schema, not docs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;api-test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the api and the schema&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;web-test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the web service and the schema&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;web-bundle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the web service (a job from the &lt;code&gt;circleci/node&lt;/code&gt; orb)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;worker-test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a matrix over two Python versions, which always runs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs-check&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;infra-validate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;infra/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;security-scan&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;everything; it is mandatory, so it always runs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;build&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;e2e&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the api; &lt;code&gt;e2e&lt;/code&gt; attaches the binary that &lt;code&gt;build&lt;/code&gt; persists&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;hold-deploy&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;deploy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;main only, after a person approves&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; every job runs, and its file reads become the impact map. On a branch only the jobs the change can reach run, plus &lt;code&gt;smarter-gate&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The demo keeps its impact map under its own cache key prefix, &lt;code&gt;smarter-demo-impact-v1&lt;/code&gt;, because the repository&amp;rsquo;s own pipeline shares the project cache. The scenarios in &lt;a href="https://github.com/CircleCI-Labs/smarter-workflows/blob/main/scripts/e2e/scenarios-demo.tsv" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;scripts/e2e/scenarios-demo.tsv&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; check what runs for each kind of change, and &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/validation/#end-to-end-scenarios"&gt;Validation&lt;/a&gt; lists the results.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>